    date "2022-07-14T09:21:35Z"
    title "Gas prices are finally going down. Will they stay below $4 a gallon?"
    description "Drivers are finally catching a break with falling gas prices in North Carolina and South Carolina. Experts say those gas prices could continue to drop across the United States, depending on a few things. &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;In this video, WCNC Charlotte's Ben Thompson connects the dots on the recent drop in gas prices and what's behind them. &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;After months of soaring gas prices, why are they going down now? AAA says the national average has fallen just under 40 cents in the past month after reaching historic highs earlier this year. In addition, the price of crude oil is below $100 a barrel for the first time in a while. This means we could see gas prices below $4 a gallon in the coming days and weeks. &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Experts as GasBuddy say the Carolinas and other Southern states will see the biggest drops. How long will it last? Officials say as long as there isn't a long-term interruption in oil production, such as a major hurricane in the Gulf of Mexico, gas prices could drop by as much as 50 cents this fall. #WakeUpCLT #Gas #GasPrices"
    channeltitle "WCNC"
    channelid "UC-RxXi2Xws6Uk22vp-sLbGA"
